WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.385
Security dashboards often contain sensitive material: video, internal addresses, usernames, facility layouts, device details, and investigation notes.

00:00:08.385 --> 00:00:13.598
Access should be based on job need, not simple convenience.

00:00:13.598 --> 00:00:19.263
Role-based access can separate operators, investigators, administrators, auditors, and read-only viewers.

00:00:19.263 --> 00:00:23.569
Apply least privilege to both people and services.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:29.688
A user who reviews endpoint alerts may not need unrestricted video access.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:36.260
A collector that submits events does not need permission to administer the dashboard.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.566
Review access regularly and remove stale accounts promptly.

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:47.592
Retention policies define how long logs, clips, thumbnails, notes, and audit records remain available.

00:00:47.592 --> 00:00:51.444
Different data types may require different periods.

00:00:51.444 --> 00:01:02.096
Keep data long enough for legitimate security, legal, and operational needs, but do not preserve sensitive material indefinitely without a defined reason.

00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:06.855
Minimize or mask data where full detail is unnecessary.

00:01:06.855 --> 00:01:17.053
A dashboard may display an event category and time without a persistent face image, or restrict raw clips to authorized review.

00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:28.158
Local-only storage can reduce external disclosure when remote processing is not required, but it still needs encryption, backup, and physical protection as appropriate.

00:01:28.158 --> 00:01:36.543
Audit logs should record sign-ins, searches, exports, configuration changes, administrative actions, and access to especially sensitive evidence.

00:01:36.543 --> 00:01:43.569
Protect those logs from casual alteration and review them for misuse or unexpected access.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:50.594
Responsible policy defines approved purposes, prohibited monitoring, notice where required, review procedures, and accountability.

00:01:50.594 --> 00:02:01.245
Do not use the dashboard for stalking, harassment, covert surveillance, or identification of private individuals without lawful authority and a legitimate need.

00:02:01.245 --> 00:02:06.911
Privacy is an architectural and operational requirement, not an optional disclaimer.
